// SOS M0 panic-seam test (design 112): the freestanding panic path is wired to
// the UART and to a failing exit.
//
// `panic(...)` lowers through the `__saw_rt_panic` seam
// (sos/rt/common_c/support.c), which writes the message through the kernel
// HAL's `sos_rt_write` and then FAILS the run via `sos_rt_abort`. The
// harness asserts the panic message appears in the output AND that the emulator
// exits with a non-zero status.
//
// The kernel core is imported for its `ktrap`, which boot.S calls: every SOS
// image links the same trap handler even when this one never reaches it.

import kcore

@export("kmain")
func kmain() {
    panic("SOS M0: deliberate panic")
}
